chunked too large: HTTP/1.1 413 Content Too Large\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 10\r\n\r\ntoo large\n
-- 100 Continue
within the limit: HTTP/1.1 100 Continue\r\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: application/octet-stream\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 5\r\n\r\nhello
over the limit: HTTP/1.1 413 Content Too Large\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 10\r\nconnection: close\r\n\r\ntoo large\n | then 
100 sent by the handler: HTTP/1.1 100 Continue\r\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: application/octet-stream\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 2\r\n\r\nok
-- informational responses
inform after respond: refused, inform: file already closed
103 and 104: HTTP/1.1 103 Early Hints\r\nlink: </style.css>; rel=preload\r\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 104 \r\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 4\r\n\r\npage
inform after respond: refused, inform: file already closed
to HTTP/1.0: HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 4\r\nconnection: close\r\n\r\npage
-- trailers
chunked: HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\nx-note: TE trailers: True\r\ndate: <date>\r\ntransfer-encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n5\r\nhello\r\n0\r\nx-checksum: abc\r\n\r\n
known length: HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\nx-note: TE trailers: False\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 5\r\n\r\nhello
event: a response was cut short: trailers were given for a body that is not chunked
request trailers: HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\ncontent-type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\ndate: <date>\r\ncontent-length: 37\r\n\r\nbefore None, after Some([(x-sum, 7)])
